{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>It is a guilt-offering.</b> Until its name is detached from it — this teaches about a guilt-offering whose owners died or whose owners achieved atonement: even though it stands for its blood to be applied to the altar's wall, if one slaughtered it without specification, it is not valid as a burnt-offering before it is detached to pasture. And it does not come to teach about the guilt-offering that it should be disqualified if not for its name — as they derived for the sin-offering from the verse — because 'it is a guilt-offering' is not said about it until after the burning of the entrails, and the offering itself whose entrails were not burned is valid (Zevaḥim 5)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:18.068487532Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}